            "\n",
            "The phrase “All but 9 die” is a concise way of saying “All of them die **except** nine of them.”  \n",
            "In English, *all but* is a set‑theoretic expression meaning “everything except.”  \n",
            "\n",
            "- **All** = the whole group (people, animals, objects, etc.)  \n",
            "- **but 9** = remove nine members from that group  \n",
            "- **die** = the fate that befalls the remaining members  \n",
            "\n",
            "So the logical structure is:\n",
            "\n",
            "```\n",
            "Group = {everyone}\n",
