            "Result = Everyone else in the group dies.\n",
            "```\n",
            "\n",
            "**Example in context**\n",
            "\n",
            "If a story says, “During the plague, all but 9 die,” it tells the reader that the plague was devastating, wiping out the entire population **except** for nine individuals who survive.\n",
            "\n",
            "**Possible uses**\n",
            "\n",
            "- **Riddles / puzzles:** The phrase can be a clue. For instance, “All but 9 die” might hint that you need to find the nine letters or numbers that *don’t* become the word “die” when transformed in some way.\n",
            "- **Statistics / reports:** A concise way to report mortality data (e.g., “In the experiment, all but 9 mice died” → 9 mice survived).\n",
            "- **Literary/poetic effect:** It emphasizes the tragedy by highlighting how few escape death.\n",
